        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Istanbul, Turkey, Topkapı Palace\n- Organizations: Eastern Orthodox Church\n- Buildings: Church of St. Mary of the Spring, Monastery of the Mother of God at the Spring, Zoödochos Pege, Hagia Irene\n- Topics: Greek and Turkish names of religious sites\n\nFacts:\n- The Monastery of the Mother of God at the Spring is also called Zoödochos Pege.\n- The Monastery of the Mother of God at the Spring has the Turkish name Balıklı Meryem Ana Rum Manastiri.\n- The Monastery of the Mother of God at the Spring is an Eastern Orthodox sanctuary in Istanbul, Turkey.\n- Hagia Irene is also known as Hagia Eirene and sometimes as Saint Irene.\n- Hagia Irene is a Greek Eastern Orthodox church in the outer courtyard of Topkapı Palace in Istanbul, Turkey.",
